<webpage>
  <title>Executive Management |NNIT</title>
  <text>
    <paragraph>Our international management team consists of eight members who are collectively responsible for running the NNIT business. Every day, they take the lead in moving our business forward and ensuring that tasks are completed and issues resolved in accordance with the Board's rules of conduct, the articles of association and all applicable laws and regulations. The management team is appointed by the Board of Directors of NNIT A/S.</paragraph>
    <paragraph>All people managers in NNIT are leading based on three core principles:</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Education:MSc in Business Administration and Economics from Linköping University, Sweden.</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Employed since:2021</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Career:Pär Fors has spent almost his entire working life in the IT industry. He began his career as a business controller and CFO and then moved into operations in various directorial roles at WM Data and Logica. In 2012, Logica became part of CGI where Pär first held the role of Managing Director, Application and Technology Services for CGI Sweden, then he became CEO of CGI Sweden and ultimately took office as CEO of CGI Scandinavia in 2019. From May 2017 to June 2021, Pär Fors was Chairman of the Board of the associationSwedish IT and Telecom Industries. He joined NNIT in June 2021.</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Read more about Pär Fors:</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Leadership</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Executive Portrait</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Education:M.Sc. in Economics &amp; Business Administration – Finance, from Aarhus School of Business, Denmark/Oregon State University, US.</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Employed since:2022</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Career:Carsten Ringius started his career as an economist in Skandia Liv in 2001 with focus on portfolio and risk management. In 2002, he joined A.P. Moller - Maersk where he held a number of leadership positions, including being responsible for Maersk finance process offshoring to service centres in India, China and the Philippines, CFO for Maersk Benelux, and Global Business Process Owner for Maersk Line Finance &amp; Accounting. In 2011, he joined TDC as divisional CFO initially for TDC Wholesale, and later as divisional CFO for TDC Nordic and TDC Erhverv, including TDC NetDesign and TDC Hosting. In 2016, he joined K.W. Bruun Import as Group CFO.</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Read more about Carsten Ringius:</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Executive Portrait</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Education:MSc in psychology and business from Roskilde University and an Executive MBA from Henley Business School.</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Employed since:June 2023Career:Prior to joining NNIT, Signe Nelsson held senior HR leadership roles within the financial and life science industries. Previously, she also acted as an Executive Advisor in the realms of public affairs and community engagement.</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Education:Graduate in Marketing Management from Copenhagen Business College. Staff Seargeant, Royal Danish Airforce.</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Employed since:August 2007</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Career:Lars B. Petersen started his career in IBM Denmark where he held a number of different positions from 1995-2007, including stationing in USA. Having begun his sales leadership career in 1997, he continued this path as sales director in NNIT in 2007. From 2011, he assumed responsibility for Marketing and Business Development; and later on he added Communications and Sustainability. As of 2023, Commercial Excellence was further added to his responsibilities. And as of 2025 he is also Head of Global Solution Development.</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Education:Bachelor – Electrical Engineering, Tianjin University (1996)Master – MBA, University of Maryland (2007)</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Employed since:October 2007</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Career:Jason Xing joined NNIT in October 2007 as the first manager hired locally in China. Jason has been central to growing the NNIT business in China both as global delivery center and local business.</paragraph>
    <paragraph>He was promoted to Corporate Vice President and NNIT China General Manger in January 2019.</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Since April 2022, Jason Xing was made responsible for the NNIT offices in China and Singapore. Before NNIT, he worked in OTIS Elevators for 4 years as Senior Manager and Motorola for 7 years as Engineer and Manager.</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Education:Master of Science, Economics (cand.polit.) from Copenhagen University</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Employed since:June 2014 (and previously from Feb. 2001- Nov. 2007)</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Career:Pia Bundgaard Ingels has beside her many years of sales and consultancy experience in NNIT worked as Senior Project Manager and Head of Projects with other IT consultancies like Valtech and T26.</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Education:MSc in Intercultural Management from Copenhagen Business School.</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Employed since:2009</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Career:Kasper started his career in NNIT in 2009, and since then he has worked his way up through six roles – from senior consultant to senior vice president and member of NNIT’s management group.</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Before he joined NNIT, he was employed in sales and project management roles at GN ReSound and IBM.</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Read more about Kasper Søndergaard Andersen:</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Leadership</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Executive Portrait</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Education:BSc in Management from Temple University.</paragraph>
    <paragraph>Employed since:November 2020 (with the acquisition of Excellis Health Solutions).Career:In addition to his previous role as CEO of Excellis Health Solutions, Greg Cathcart has comprehensive experience from chief and sales executive roles within the life sciences industry, including Johnson &amp; Johnson and SAP.</paragraph>
